    <string name="about">About</string>
    <string name="about_text">Screen Translator %1$s — no ads, no tracking, no payments.</string>
    <string name="tips">Tips: tap the bubble to translate the full screen, double-tap to select a region, long-press for the menu, drag to move. Tap a translated box for details, copy, read aloud or dictionary. Swipe up to close the translation. Select text in any app and choose \"Translate\" for quick text translation.</string>
    <string name="need_overlay">Grant \"Display over other apps\" and tap again.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_body">1. Home: type, paste, speak or handwrite for instant translation. Tap a language to change it, ⇄ to swap. Star ★ to save to the Phrasebook.\n\n2. Shortcuts: Camera (live), Handwriting, Conversation (two people), Transcribe (long speech), Screen translation, Image translation.\n\n3. Screen translation: grant \"Display over other apps\", then start the bubble. Tap = whole screen, double-tap = select a region, long-press = menu.\n\n4. Tap to Translate: turn it on in the menu, then copy text in any app to get a quick translation card.\n\n5. Offline out of the box: Chinese, English, Vietnamese (downloaded on first run). Other languages are in \"Offline language packs\". When online, Google Translate is used for better quality.\n\n6. Floating icon keeps closing? Settings → \"Keep the floating icon alive\".</string>
    <string name="privacy_body">• No ads, no analytics, no payments, no tracking SDKs.\n• Default translation mode is \"Automatic\": WHEN ONLINE the text you translate is sent to Google Translate (a public web endpoint, no account) for the best quality; OFFLINE, or when you pick \"ML Kit\", everything stays on the device. To send nothing out, choose ML Kit in Settings → Translation engine.\n• Tap to Translate reads the clipboard only when you enable it and skips content flagged as sensitive.\n• Accessibility: screenshots, reading visible text (Accessibility mode) and — only if you enable it — translating as you type. Password fields are always skipped. Your actions are not recorded.\n• Microphone: used only by Transcribe; Conversation and voice input use the system speech recognizer.\n• History and Phrasebook are stored on the device only and can be cleared anytime.</string>
